## Getting started

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.11+
- Docker and Docker Compose
- A [Groq API key](https://console.groq.com/keys)

### 1. Clone and install

```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd <repo-folder>

python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate

python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

`requirements.txt` should include:

```
fastapi
uvicorn[standard]
python-multipart
pydantic-settings
sqlalchemy
psycopg2-binary
qdrant-client
redis
openai
pypdf
email-validator
sentence-transformers
```

> The Groq endpoint is OpenAI-compatible, so the `openai` SDK is used with a custom `base_url`.
> The first run downloads the embedding model (about 90 MB) from Hugging Face.

### 2. Start infrastructure

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

This starts Qdrant (`6333`), Redis (`6379`) and PostgreSQL (`5432`).

### 3. Configure environment

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your key:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

```env
# LLM (Groq)
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key
GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
CHAT_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# Embeddings (local)
EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
EMBEDDING_DIM=384

# Infrastructure
QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
QDRANT_COLLECTION=documents
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://app:app@localhost:5432/app

# Chat memory
CHAT_HISTORY_LIMIT=10
SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=3600
```

Adjust the variable names if your `config.py` uses different ones.

> **Important:** `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` produces **384-dimensional** vectors. If you previously created the Qdrant collection with a different size (for example 1536 for OpenAI embeddings), delete the collection or the Qdrant volume and let the app recreate it, otherwise upserts will fail.
>
> ```bash
> curl -X DELETE http://localhost:6333/collections/documents
> ```

### 4. Run the server

```bash
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

Interactive docs: <http://localhost:8000/docs>

